Both licenses permit use, modification and redistribution; binaries
include both license texts (run "hmbridge -license"). Michael Stapelberg
does not endorse this fork; the BSD-3-Clause license forbids using his name
to promote derived products.

Protocol knowledge comes from FHEM, Homegear and RFNETHM (all GPL); no code
from these projects is included. The AES test vectors in
internal/bidcos/aes/testdata were produced by running FHEM's code; they are
data, not code.
